==Strategy==
The main threat of this stage are the three waves of high-magnification Duches and Dagshunds. The Zombie enemies don't pose much of a threat: they instead serve as meatshields. The use of Zombies as peons, paired with the large waves of Duches and Dagshunds, makes this stage cash tight.

With the help of Starting Money UP [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]], this stage can be cheesed with [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. This is the preferred strategy on 3-Crown difficulty.

If you have to fight the waves head on, prepare for a long fight. Due to the cash-tight nature of the stage, money-boosting Cat Combos are recommended. Units that provide [[:Category:1-Slot Combos|1-slot]] money combos, like [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Richest Cat]] and [[Kunio-kun (Uber Rare Cat)|Kunio-kun]] can be brought to great effect. Use [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] to better deal with the peons as well as strong and spammable [[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|midrangers]], with [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] in particular being a solid choice. [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] is recommended to help stop the [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies from pushing, especially on 4-Crown.

